{block beforeContent}
<div class="container">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="p-5 text-white bg-dark">
                <h3>Downloads</h3>
                <p class="lead">Here you can download the SmartCGMS software framework, utilities and datasets.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
{/block}

{block content}

<div class="row">
    <div class="col-12">
        <h3>SmartCGMS</h3>

        <p>When publishing any results obtained using SmartCGMS, you must include the following citation:
            <ol>
                <li><i>T. Koutny and M. Ubl, "SmartCGMS as a Testbed for a Blood-Glucose Level Prediction and/or Control Challenge with (an FDA-Accepted) Diabetic Patient Simulation", Procedia Computer Science, Volume 177, pp. 354-362, 2020</i></li>
            </ol>
        </p>
        
        <p>
            <a n:href="Downloads:smartcgms" class="btn btn-dark"><i class="bi bi-input-cursor"></i> Download SmartCGMS</a>
        </p>
        
        <h3>Open Source</h3>    
        <p>If you would like to stay on the "bleeding-edge", you can <a href="https://github.com/SmartCGMS/" title="SmartCGMS on GitHub">download SmartCGMS from GitHub</a> so that you can build it yourself.</p>
    </div>
</div>
    
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-12">
        <h3>Enriched glucose-level database</h3>

        <p>When publishing any results obtained with this database, you must include the following citations:</p>
        <p><i>We have used a database with diabetes type-1 completely anonymized CGMS profiles, which is available as a part of the SmartCGMS project [1]. This database has been enriched with artificially calculated blood glucose levels [2].
                <ol>
                    <li>T. Koutny and M. Ubl, "SmartCGMS as a Testbed for a Blood-Glucose Level Prediction and/or Control Challenge with (an FDA-Accepted) Diabetic Patient Simulation", Procedia Computer Science, Volume 177, pp. 354-362, 2020</i></li>
                    <li>I. De Falco, A. Della Cioppa, A. Giugliano, A. Marcelli, T. Koutny, M. Krcma, U. Scafuri, E. Tarantino, "A Genetic Programming-based Regression for Extrapolating a Blood Glucose-Dynamics Model from Interstitial Glucose Measurements and their Derivatives", Submitted to the Applied Soft Computing Journal, 2018</li>
                </ol>
            </i>
        </p>
        
        <p>
            <a n:href="Downloads:dataset" class="btn btn-dark"><i class="bi bi-input-cursor"></i> Download database</a>
        </p>
        
        <h3>Open Source</h3>    
        <p>If you would like to stay on the "bleeding-edge", you can <a href="https://github.com/SmartCGMS/" title="SmartCGMS on GitHub">download SmartCGMS from GitHub</a> so that you can build it yourself.</p>
    </div>
</div>
    
<div class="row">
    <div class="col-12">
        <h3>Icarus has diabetes</h3>
        
        <p>Here you can download the Icarus has diabetes game. It is currently available for MS Windows only.</p>
        
        <p>
            <a n:href="downloadIcarus!" class="btn btn-dark">Download Icarus has diabetes</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</div>

{/block}
    